<body><main class="shell">
<nav class="top"><a href="./">← Chloe reads Jon</a><span>Field experiment No. 206 · 20 Oct 2026</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">An exceedingly small disaster laboratory</div><h1>Memory<br><em>Lifeboat.</em></h1><p class="intro">The laptop can be replaced.<br>The cardboard-robot birthday cannot.</p></div><aside><span class="stamp">Handle with care</span><p>Three albums. Nine storage credits.<br>Give your memories somewhere else to live.</p><p class="tiny">Tap destinations to add or remove copies. Then throw a little fictional chaos at your plan. Nothing is uploaded; these are illustrated pretend albums.</p></aside></header>
<section class="photos" aria-label="The three illustrated albums you are protecting">
<article class="photo"><div class="scene" role="img" aria-label="Paper collage of a canoe on a mountain lake"></div><div class="caption">The lake weekend <small>ALBUM 01</small></div></article>
<article class="photo"><div class="scene" role="img" aria-label="Paper collage of a cardboard robot and birthday cake"></div><div class="caption">Robot birthday <small>ALBUM 02</small></div></article>
<article class="photo"><div class="scene" role="img" aria-label="Paper collage of a train beside the sea"></div><div class="caption">The coastal train <small>ALBUM 03</small></div></article>
</section>
<noscript><p class="noscript">Enable JavaScript to place copies and run the survival experiments.</p></noscript>
<section class="board" aria-labelledby="build-title"><div class="bar"><div><div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold)">01 / Build the lifeboats</div><h2 id="build-title">One copy is a single point of heartbreak.</h2></div><div class="budget"><strong id="credits">9</strong> / 9 left<progress id="meter" max="9" value="9" aria-label="Storage credits remaining"></progress></div></div><div id="collections" class="collections"></div><p id="notice" class="board-note" role="status">Every album starts on the laptop. Extra copies cost credits, not real money.</p></section>
<section class="legend" aria-label="How each destination works"><div><h3>Desk drive · 1 credit</h3><p>An unplugged, independent disk at home. Safe from sync deletions, not home theft.</p></div><div><h3>Off-site drive · 1 credit</h3><p>An independent disk at a friend’s house. Different location, same drive medium as the desk disk.</p></div><div><h3>Cloud sync · 1 credit</h3><p>An off-site mirror. Delete an album on the laptop and the deletion travels here too.</p></div><div><h3>Versioned backup · 2 credits</h3><p>Off-site cloud snapshots with retained history. Can restore an earlier version after deletion.</p></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="test-title"><div class="testhead"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Try some very bad luck</div><h2 id="test-title">Will the memories make it?</h2></div><button id="reset">Start over ↺</button></div><p class="tiny">Each test starts from your intact plan. Disasters do not stack. You can change your copies while a test is open.</p><div class="incidents" id="incidents"></div><div class="report" id="report" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" id="all">Run all four tests →</button><button id="print">Print my rescue plan</button></div></section>
<section class="lesson"><div class="numbers">3 · 2 · 1</div><div><p><strong>The useful little rule:</strong> three copies, on two storage media, with one copy off-site. Here the laptop, physical backup disks, and cloud count as three media categories.</p><p class="tiny">A mirror is not a time machine. Three copies can meet the numbers and still share a deletion risk. Independent copies, retained versions, and actually testing a restore are what make a plan useful.</p><p class="tiny">Try protecting every album from all four incidents AND earning all three checkmarks, without overspending. There is more than one solution.</p></div></section>
<footer class="footer"><p>Inspired by Jon’s <a href="?source=1">Photo Storage Strategy</a>, a 2014 post about making room for family photographs while keeping them backed up.</p><p>This is a simplified game, not a backup service. In real life, retention limits, stale copies, account access, encryption keys, and failed restores matter too. These illustrated memories are fictional. Original collage created with GPT Image.</p></footer>
</main><script>
'use strict';
const albums=['The lake weekend','Robot birthday','The coastal train'];
const places=[
{id:'desk',name:'Desk drive',cost:1,medium:'disk',offsite:false},
{id:'away',name:'Off-site drive',cost:1,medium:'disk',offsite:true},
{id:'sync',name:'Cloud sync',cost:1,medium:'cloud',offsite:true},
{id:'vault',name:'Versioned backup',cost:2,medium:'cloud',offsite:true}
];
const incidents=[
{name:'The tea spill',icon:'01',dead:['laptop'],story:'One enthusiastic elbow. One very wet laptop. The extra copies are untouched.',lesson:'A separate disk is already a huge improvement over a single laptop.'},
{name:'The home burglary',icon:'02',dead:['laptop','desk'],story:'The laptop and the desk drive leave together. Copies outside the house are still there.',lesson:'Two devices in the same room can share one disaster. Off-site means somewhere else.'},
{name:'The mistaken delete',icon:'03',dead:['laptop','sync'],story:'An album is deleted on the laptop. Cloud sync faithfully mirrors the mistake. Independent disks and retained backup versions keep their copies.',lesson:'Sync is wonderfully obedient. That is precisely the problem when the instruction was a mistake.'},
{name:'The cloud outage',icon:'04',dead:['sync','vault'],story:'Both cloud destinations are unreachable right now. Local and off-site disks still work. Cloud copies are unavailable, not necessarily destroyed.',lesson:'Availability matters too. A copy you can open without the provider keeps the afternoon moving.'}
];
let copies=albums.map(()=>new Set(['laptop'])),active=null;
const byId=id=>document.getElementById(id);
function spent(){return copies.reduce((sum,s)=>sum+places.filter(p=>s.has(p.id)).reduce((n,p)=>n+p.cost,0),0)}
function rules(s){return [s.size>=3,new Set(['computer',...places.filter(p=>s.has(p.id)).map(p=>p.medium)]).size>=2,places.some(p=>s.has(p.id)&&p.offsite)]}
function survivors(s,i){return [...s].filter(p=>!incidents[i].dead.includes(p))}
function render(){
 byId('credits').textContent=9-spent();byId('meter').value=9-spent();
 byId('collections').innerHTML=albums.map((name,a)=>'<article class="collection"><h3>'+name+'</h3><div class="original">▣ Laptop original · included</div><div class="places">'+places.map(p=>'<button class="place" data-album="'+a+'" data-place="'+p.id+'" aria-label="'+p.name+' for '+name+'" aria-pressed="'+copies[a].has(p.id)+'"><span>'+p.name+'</span><span>'+(copies[a].has(p.id)?'✓ copied':'+ '+p.cost)+'</span></button>').join('')+'</div><p class="checks">'+rules(copies[a]).map((yes,i)=>'<span class="'+(yes?'yes':'')+'">'+(yes?'✓':'○')+' '+['3 copies','2 media','1 off-site'][i]+'</span>').join(' · ')+'</p></article>').join('');
 document.querySelectorAll('.incident').forEach((b,i)=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',active===i));
 report();
}
function report(){
 const box=byId('report');
 if(active===null){box.innerHTML='<h3>Your albums are waiting for a plot twist.</h3><p>Choose an incident above, or run the complete inspection. Your plan stays editable.</p>';return}
 if(active==='all'){
 let passed=incidents.filter((_,i)=>copies.every(s=>survivors(s,i).length)).length;
 let marks=copies.every(s=>rules(s).every(Boolean));
 box.innerHTML='<h3>'+passed+' / 4 incidents survived by every album</h3><p>'+(passed===4&&marks?'Lifeboat certified. Every album meets 3–2–1, and every fictional restore has a surviving route.':passed===4?'All four restores work. Now see whether every album can earn its 3–2–1 checkmarks too.':'Some memories have no surviving route. Inspect the individual incidents, move a few copies, and try again.')+'</p><div class="restores">'+incidents.map((d,i)=>'<div class="restore '+(copies.every(s=>survivors(s,i).length)?'':'lost')+'"><strong>'+d.name+'</strong>'+copies.filter(s=>survivors(s,i).length).length+' / 3 albums recoverable</div>').join('')+'</div>';return;
 }
 const d=incidents[active],labels={laptop:'laptop',desk:'desk drive',away:'off-site drive',sync:'cloud sync',vault:'retained backup version'};
 box.innerHTML='<h3>'+d.name+'</h3><p>'+d.story+'</p><div class="restores">'+copies.map((s,a)=>{let safe=survivors(s,active);return '<div class="restore '+(!safe.length?'lost':'')+'"><strong>'+albums[a]+'</strong>'+(safe.length?'✓ Restore from '+safe.map(p=>labels[p]).join(' or '):'× No accessible copy in this test')+'</div>'}).join('')+'</div><p class="tiny" style="margin-bottom:0">'+d.lesson+'</p>';
}
byId('collections').addEventListener('click',e=>{
 let b=e.target.closest('button[data-place]');if(!b)return;
 const a=Number(b.dataset.album),p=places.find(p=>p.id===b.dataset.place);
 const focusLabel=b.getAttribute('aria-label');
 if(copies[a].has(p.id)){copies[a].delete(p.id);byId('notice').textContent='Copy removed. Credits returned to your budget.'}
 else if(spent()+p.cost>9){byId('notice').textContent='Not enough credits. Remove another copy to free up space.';return}
 else{copies[a].add(p.id);byId('notice').textContent=albums[a]+' copied to '+p.name.toLowerCase()+'.'}
 render();[...document.querySelectorAll('.place')].find(b=>b.getAttribute('aria-label')===focusLabel).focus({preventScroll:true});
});
byId('incidents').innerHTML=incidents.map((d,i)=>'<button class="incident" data-test="'+i+'" aria-pressed="false"><b>'+d.icon+'</b>'+d.name+'</button>').join('');
byId('incidents').addEventListener('click',e=>{let b=e.target.closest('button');if(b){active=Number(b.dataset.test);render()}});
byId('all').addEventListener('click',()=>{active='all';render()});
byId('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{copies=albums.map(()=>new Set(['laptop']));active=null;byId('notice').textContent='Fresh start. Nine credits and three laptop originals.';render()});
byId('print').addEventListener('click',()=>{
 const old=active;active='all';render();
 let plan=document.createElement('section');plan.id='printplan';plan.innerHTML='<h2>Your copy locations</h2>'+albums.map((name,a)=>'<p><strong>'+name+':</strong> laptop'+places.filter(p=>copies[a].has(p.id)).map(p=>', '+p.name).join('')+'</p>').join('');
 byId('report').append(plan);window.print();plan.remove();active=old;render();
});
render();
</script></body></html>
